# Vulnerabilities accepted, for a bounded time, in the Gotenberg image pinned by
# docker-compose.gotenberg.yml. Gate: script/gates/cve_accepted_diff.sh, run nightly by
# .github/workflows/gotenberg-cve.yml.
#
# Format, one record per line:
#
#     ADVISORY-ID | valid-through (YYYY-MM-DD) | why it is accepted
#
# Blank lines and `#` lines are ignored. Every field is validated and a malformed record
# FAILS the gate rather than being skipped: an acceptance whose date does not parse is an
# acceptance that never expires, and this project already has a rule about things that
# never expire.
#
# --- WHY THIS FILE EXISTS AT ALL ------------------------------------------------------
#
# The scan was `trivy --exit-code 1` first, and on its first real run it went red and
# STAYED red for a reason it had no way to say. MEASURED 2026-08-10: the pinned image has
# five fixable HIGH findings across four advisories, and `gotenberg/gotenberg:8` and
# `gotenberg/gotenberg:8.35.0` BOTH resolve to the digest already pinned — 8.35.0 being
# the newest tag upstream publishes. The workflow's own remediation ("move the pin")
# named an action that did not exist.
#
# A gate nobody can satisfy gets switched off, and a gate switched off is worse than no
# gate — INV-4. Making it advisory is forbidden in the other direction (CLAUDE.md §7). So
# the gate stays a gate and the exceptions are enumerated here, each dated, each with a
# reason. What the gate then refuses is:
#
#   1. a fixable HIGH/CRITICAL this file does not name  — a new vulnerability
#   2. an entry whose valid-through date has passed     — an acceptance nobody re-examined
#   3. an entry the scan no longer reports              — a stale exemption; delete it
#
# (3) is what stops this file becoming permanent furniture, and it is the same assertion
# zero_reporter.allowlist above it lives under: THIS LIST MAY ONLY SHRINK, except when a
# newly published vulnerability is consciously accepted with a date.
#
# --- WHAT `valid-through` MEANS -------------------------------------------------------
#
# Not a prediction of when a fix lands. It is the date somebody must LOOK AGAIN: has
# upstream rebuilt, and is the reason on the record still true? Thirty days makes that a
# nightly build going red once a month rather than a calendar entry nobody keeps.
#
# ======================================================================================
# Gotenberg 8.35.0 — digest a16a14e1f18a71405624bc028e90d4ef50ea774c352b303639c10bf7b141f760
# ======================================================================================
#
# ALL FOUR ENTRIES SHARE THE REASON ABOVE: there is nowhere to move the pin to. The Debian
# fixes exist; a Gotenberg image carrying them does not.
#
# WHAT CONTAINS THEM MEANWHILE is in docker-compose.gotenberg.yml and is not rhetorical:
# `internal: true` (no route off the network), a non-root user with Chromium's own sandbox
# left ON, a read-only root filesystem, `cap_drop: ALL`, `no-new-privileges`, and the
# LibreOffice and PDF-engine routes switched off. None of that fixes a use-after-free. It
# decides what an attacker reaches after one.

# THE ONE THAT MATTERS, because Chromium is the render path — the process that parses a
# report's HTML. A sandbox escape means the containment above is all that is left, which
# is exactly why the compose file refuses `--no-sandbox` and keeps the container non-root.
CVE-2026-19155 | 2026-09-09 | chromium/chromium-common 151.0.7922.71: sandbox escape via use-after-free in Payments; fixed in 151.0.7922.108-1~deb13u1, which no published Gotenberg image contains.

# THE THREE IN `usr/bin/pdfcpu`, reachable only through the PDF-engine routes — which the
# documented compose file starts the container WITHOUT (`--pdfengines-disable-routes`), so
# neither this plugin nor anyone following the example reaches the code. That is a
# mitigation and NOT an argument that the finding is wrong: Trivy scans the image, and an
# operator who drops that flag gets the exposure back.
CVE-2026-46602 | 2026-09-09 | pdfcpu / golang.org/x/image v0.41.0: unbounded allocation decoding a TIFF; fixed in 0.43.0. Unreachable with --pdfengines-disable-routes.
CVE-2026-46604 | 2026-09-09 | pdfcpu / golang.org/x/image v0.41.0: panic decoding an invalid TIFF; fixed in 0.43.0. Unreachable with --pdfengines-disable-routes.
CVE-2026-56852 | 2026-09-09 | pdfcpu / golang.org/x/text v0.37.0: denial of service on invalid UTF-8 input; fixed in 0.39.0. Unreachable with --pdfengines-disable-routes.
